      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Dust storms in the 1930s buried farms and homes, prompting many families to abandon their land or seek relief through federal programs.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/lewis_kansas",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Winters bring about 17 inches of snowfall annually, while summers are marked by intense solar heating, high winds, and high evaporation rates that require irrigation.",
